. On the other hand, $f(x)$ has vertical asymptotes at $x=-7$ and $x=0.$ These asymptotes divide the number line into $3$ subintervals:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,-7),\\,(-7,0),\\,(0,\\infty )\n$$\n\nNow, we construct a sign table with the list of intervals on the top and the list of factors on the left. Filling in the sign table using the usual method, we get the following result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-7)$ | $(-7,0)$ | $(0,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $x+7$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $-4$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the inequality $f(x)>0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where $f(x)$ is positive.\n\nFrom the table, we see that $f(x)$ is positive on the intervals $(-7,0).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\nf(x)>0\\,\\text{for all}\\,x\\in (\\,-7,0\\,).\n$$" 13194139534498 true] [17592186292010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292011 13194139534498 true] [17592186292010 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534498 true] [17592186292010 1041 "field-1" 13194139534498 true] [17592186292010 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292011 13194139534498 true] [17592186292010 1110 #uuid "a9a2e99e-04d1-5af4-9ac9-11511cedbb54" 13194139534498 true] [17592186292011 1034 "-7" 13194139534498 true] [17592186292011 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534498 true] [17592186292011 1111 #uuid "86fba9fe-b851-53ff-bba5-901e30b09e60" 13194139534498 true] [17592186292012 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292013 13194139534498 true] [17592186292012 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534498 true] [17592186292012 1041 "field-2" 13194139534498 true] [17592186292012 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292013 13194139534498 true] [17592186292012 1110 #uuid "2d9ba9e3-863e-54c1-94f5-15d108007a0d" 13194139534498 true] [17592186292013 1034 "0" 13194139534498 true] [17592186292013 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534498 true] [17592186292013 1111 #uuid "78112087-3dee-5a7e-a2d2-329c9990c632" 13194139534498 true] [17592186292014 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292015 13194139534